ot the WP publisher**.\n\n### Why WordPress has the image\nThe WP publisher works differently:\n- it takes `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` directly\n- uploads it to WordPress\n- sets it as the featured image there\n\nSo WordPress can still have the image even if the Drive doc missed it.\n\n### Why Google Drive missed the image\nThe Drive version depends on this **Step 4 preprocessing block**:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg ] && [ $(stat -c%s /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg 2>/dev/null || echo 0) -gt 10000 ]; then\n    printf '![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\\n\\n' | cat - /tmp/crypto-article.md > /tmp/crypto-with-image.md\n    echo \"[IMAGE] Embedded valid feature image.\"\nelse\n    cp /tmp/crypto-article.md /tmp/crypto-with-image.md\n    echo \"[IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.\"\nfi\n```\n\nThat block is the **actual culprit**.\n\n### Proof\nYou already have the smoking gun:\n- the export log said: **`[IMAGE] No valid feature image found, skipping embedding.`**\n- and `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md` started directly with `META`, not with:\n  `![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)`\n\nThat means the image was dropped **before pandoc** ever made the DOCX.\n\nSo the failure chain is:\n\n1. creator generated the image successfully ✅  \n2. wp-publisher used that image directly ✅  \n3. Drive export step incorrectly decided the image was “not valid” ❌  \n4. `/tmp/crypto-with-image.md` was created without the image ❌  \n5. pandoc converted that image-less markdown into DOCX ❌  \n6. Drive upload faithfully uploaded the image-less DOCX ❌\n\n### Bottom line\nThe thing to fix is:\n\n**the Drive export image-embed check in Step 4**, not the creator, not the WP publisher, and not the Drive uploader.\n\nIf you want the shortest possible diagnosis to keep in mind:\n\n> **WP uses the JPEG directly; Drive only gets whatever Step 4 embeds into markdown first. Step 4 skipped the embed, so Drive never h